WEBVTT

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.090
He did it! That damn Joe!

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:29.250
He finally used For the Sake of Tomorrow #3!

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.250
He did it!

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.100
Bro Joe!

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.350
Rikiishi-san!

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.380
Wh-What just happened!?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.490
Rikiishi-san!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.890
1!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.420
2!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.110
3!

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.620
Stop it!

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.620
Don't you get it? There's no point in counting.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.660
Whether we wait ten seconds or thirty minutes...

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.840
No, even if we wait an hour, neither of them will stand up.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.900
What's so funny?

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.370
Damn you, old man!

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.860
Y-You bastard! You probably rigged this, didn't you?

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.910
Yeah, that's right! As if we'd believe your nonsense!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:43.670
Hey, old fart!

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:48.330
You probably used some sort of black magic on Rikiishi-san!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.050
Black magic...

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:54.330
Maybe it would seem that way to you.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.920
Yeah, we probably shouldn't move those two right now.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.130
That way, I can explain everything while they sleep.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.180
You... Do you know about "Seki Mitsunori" and "Fighting Harada"?

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.680
Of course I do!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.400
They're both Japanese boxing legends.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.140
Wh-What does th-that have to do with this?

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.630
There was a man who defeated each of them with a single punch.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.650
That man,

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.850
was the Mexican champion, Medel; feared whenever he went near the ropes.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.870
Seki and Harada had pushed Medel right up against the ropes,

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.370
but suddenly

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.360
Medel gave them an explosive punch.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:43.380
With just that one punch, each of them ended up in a coma.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.230
Seki and Harada were each taken down by one punch?

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.430
A-Are you saying Joe used the same punch?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.490
That's right!

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.680
Joe used the same thing.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.920
He used the greatest technique in boxing!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.440
The cross counter!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.940
C-Cross counter?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.440
C-Cross counter!?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.940
Cross counter...

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.700
That's right! The cross counter!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.620
In other words, strike when you are about to be hit.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.060
Cut the flesh and break the bones.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.450
Strike with a deadly punch at the same time.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.340
You hit the opponent as he moves to hit you with all his power.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.980
Your punch's power is doubled since it gains the power of <i>his</i> punch.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.800
Not to mention,

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.260
during a cross counter,

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.160
you slide your arm over your opponent's, gaining leverage.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.030
This can triple or even quadruple your punch's power.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.820
Just thinking of it is terrifying!

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:40.730
On top of all that, Joe used the ropes as a spring.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.550
No one, not even Rikiishi-kun, could have withstood it.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:56.710
In Joe's case, it was a lucky punch. Pure luck.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.430
I was thinking about Rikiishi-kun before the match...

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.900
I thought he might keep pounding Joe and win easily.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.970
But for Joe, that was his greatest strength.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:12.510
<i>Joe! There is only one way for you to defeat Rikiishi!</i>

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.920
Using my own body, I taught Joe how to use the cross counter.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.810
And, as you gentlemen know,

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.400
Joe's special training began from there.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:37.140
But, being a renowned pro boxer,

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.040
Rikiishi-kun saw through my plan.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.920
He then developed a plan of his own,

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:47.590
to attack Joe's openings as Joe rushed to hit him.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.380
If he succeeded, Joe wouldn't stand a chance.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:58.430
So, with a heavy heart, I asked for the match to continue regardless of the number of knockdowns.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:02.060
This way, if Joe could survive the blood,

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:06.360
as well as the countless knockdowns he would take until near death,

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.900
and still manage to get back onto his feet,

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.170
then when he got up, Rikiishi-kun would have no choice but to go for a finishing blow.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.220
I bet everything on that moment.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.250
And, in the end, we won!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.500
It should be fine for me to say we won.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:56.630
After all, a complete amateur fought a pro and ended the fight in a draw.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.460
I said it was pure luck before,

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:06.290
but it was also due to Joe's unwavering will to get back up after each knockdown.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:07.910
Joe!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:23.670
I've lived my life running from one place to another.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.230
I've been hated by many people, and sank so low to live in the slums,

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.740
but from the bottom of my heart, I'm so glad to be alive!

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.190
Isn't that right, my Joe!?

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:38.580
Joe!

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.490
Danpei-san,

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.550
do you have a moment?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.260
Sure.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:01.990
What is it?

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:07.000
We were planning to hold a tournament amongst the inmates,

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.250
but after witnessing the tragic conclusion of the earlier match,

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.150
the inmates are all nervous.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:16.210
Let's not have another match today, okay?

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.850
It would be unfortunate to see any more people injured.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.700
Next time, we will—

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.010
Wh-What is that?

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.480
Warden, over there!

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.490
Wh-What!? What's going on!?

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.000
What do you think you're doing, you bastard!?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.500
Stop it, you stupid pervert!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.630
M-Me too! I want to be in the tournament!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.800
Shut up! What can a weak little bug like you do?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.550
Be a good boy and go away!

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.670
I can still fight! Give me the gloves!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.510
Someone as weak as you should stay outside the ring!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.190
Boxing is not a show or a fight,

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.430
it's a sport!

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:11.450
I can still do it!

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:12.860
Get out of my way!

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.680
Wh-What's the meaning of this?

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.990
What h-has been started?

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:25.620
I... I think I can understand their feelings.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.120
They were truly impressed by what they saw.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.130
I-Impressed?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.820
That's right, they were impressed.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.260
That amazing match between Rikiishi and Joe... That fight between two men.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.690
Watching how Joe kept getting back up, even when he was covered in blood,

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:48.610
and the cross counter that knocked them both out...

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.640
That deeply moved them.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.060
Moreover, behind the obvious differences between them,

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:59.900
were great plans, theories, and techniques.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.530
"Boxing isn't brute strength.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:04.300
If I have the will, even I can do it!"

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:10.140
I believe that's the powerful, manly instinct that has driven them to this.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:13.040
They were deeply moved emotionally, not just logically.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.540
I-I'm going to join in too!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:23.160
What an unexpected outcome...

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.940
So, how are we supposed to handle this?

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:29.020
I'd like to hear your opinion, Miss, as you're the sponsor of the boxing tournament.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:33.280
I only asked my grandfather to donate some boxing gear.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:37.520
At this point, I have nothing to say.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:45.030
That said, I'm surprised at this outcome, too.

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:47.910
Here, take a look!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.150
The order has already been decided!

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.540
The tournament will now begin.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.590
The decided opponents will fight in order.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.090
Nishi-kun is the referee, huh?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.590
N-Never mind that, isn't that little guy over there Aoyama!?

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.620
Aoyama!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.030
If you want to back out, this is your chance!

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:15.600
Don't blame us if you die!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.520
R-Ridiculous! Is he seriously going to fight?

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:19.800
L-Let's stop it.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.110
Hold it!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:31.120
Warden, do you not understand a man's alternating hope and fear?{TLC. No I do not understand "a man's alternating hope and fear"}

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:35.020
But... But, you see... Aoyama's opponent, Arai, is really violent.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.620
If anything happens to him...

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:40.300
A fire has been lit in little Aoyama's heart.

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:44.010
Instead of trying to extinguish it,

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:47.630
won't you watch his burning flame?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.650
Ring the gong!

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.150
Right! Leave it to me!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.880
Aoyama! If you're going for it, at least make it enjoyable for us!

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.320
Hurry up and knock out that Aoyama weakling!

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.850
I got it, I got it.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:16.830
But before that, I want to do what Rikiishi-san did.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.450
You probably can't tell since I'm wearing my gloves,

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:25.710
but I'm pointing my index finger.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:29.440
It won't be the first round, or even the first minute,

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.150
but just one second!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:33.640
One second is all the time I need to take this weakling down!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.180
Hey, Aoyama!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:38.200
The gong has been rung, so you can hit him.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:40.440
A-All right!

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:47.440
Hey, Aoyama, you always cry when I hit you, right?

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.310
Arai, what happened?

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.200
He's not half bad!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:02.080
I... I took him down... w-with my punch!

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:03.920
1!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.170
2!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.990
3!

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.990
You really did it!

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:07.710
How dare you!?

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:09.800
Hold it!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:14.240
You need to get the tar from the floor off your gloves.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.220
Shut up, let me go!

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.210
Do you think I'm some blind old dumbass!?

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:22.230
If you won't listen to the referee, you'll be disqualified!

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:25.730
Okay.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.230
Hey, Arai! What happened to taking him down in one second?

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.170
Did you mean <i>you'd</i> get knocked down in one second?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.940
All right, we will now resume the match.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:35.740
Fight!

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.240
Damn you, Aoyama. I won't go easy on you this time!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.360
S-Strong little guy, isn't he!?

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.800
Go, go, Aoyama! Knock him down again!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:04.310
You bastard!

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:08.780
Wait!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.300
You...

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:16.560
That was dirty, you bastard!

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.660
You rang the gong right when Aoyama was open!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.970
Boxing has rules, you know!

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.660
Go rest, Aoyama.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:26.330
D-Damn it! You damn piece of...

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.390
Arai! The first round is already over!

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:30.250
Can't you win?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:31.850
Shut up! Just wait and see!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.260
I'll finish this with one punch!

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.500
Arai! Which punch will end the match?

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.700
You don't have a clue, do you?

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:41.720
What do you think of those cheerful inmates' faces?

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:46.310
They're all engrossed in this, aren't they, Miss?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:47.630
Miss...

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:56.590
There is no doubt. No doubt whatsoever. This is all so unexpected.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:17:01.290
I've never seen them this happy and excited.

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.580
Of course, everyone was pleased with my performance,

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:12.460
but was that joy from the bottom of their hearts?

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:22.880
They called me "Sunday's Angel,"

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.520
just because I came to this island every week.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:32.650
<i>Miss,</i>

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:37.840
<i>you do all these things in a condescending way, as though you come from above the clouds.</i>

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.700
<i>Boxing.</i>

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.840
<i>This time, it's preachings from some almighty god?</i>

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.290
No... That's not true, not true!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.950
What's wrong?

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.800
Don't you want to watch the boxing match, kids?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.340
I don't want to watch weak fighters.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:05.760
Just looking at them will hurt our eyes.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:17.780
What's wrong, Aoyama? What happened to the spirit you had?

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:22.220
It's cowardly to run away!

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:23.160
Wait!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.190
I-I'm not running away!

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:28.410
I'm just doing what Yabuki-san did!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.500
You bastard, looking down on me!

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.980
I can barely feel your punches through those gloves!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.210
How was that? Giving up yet?

00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:00.950
These gloves are really heavy!

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.780
It seems like you're finally tired out!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.980
You bastard! How dare you look down on me...

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.200
Damn you!

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:11.760
Aoyama's really pissed off Arai now!

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.000
Eat this!

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:18.710
Cross counter!

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:27.090
He did it!

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:29.060
Way to go, Aoyama!

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.570
You're really awesome, Aoyama!

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:32.060
Nice!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:38.820
It's not quite like Yabuki-san's cross counter, but the principle is the same.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.630
1!

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:41.820
2!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.780
Arai, that was pathetic. Was that all just talk?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.800
That's right!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.330
This is my chance to get revenge for all his bullying.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:52.730
I'll deliver a finishing blow with all my strength!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.420
You...

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.430
H-Hey, you!

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:57.880
That's against the rules! You'll be disqualified!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.840
B-But... this is the perfect chance to get him!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.740
This isn't some brawl!

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:05.830
This is boxing! Now, go back to a neutral corner!

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:14.010
Th-These gloves are restricting my punches.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.060
Damn it.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.270
Hey! Hold it!

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:22.610
You, too! This is boxing, not a brawl!

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:23.110
You bastard!

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.380
Put your gloves back on!

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.160
N-No!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.620
I don't care what you say, I'll take him down with my bare fists!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.870
Damn!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.760
I-Idiot! What are you doing!?

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:35.600
Hey! Wh—

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.690
We're boxing here!

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.370
You took off your gloves in the middle of a boxing match!

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.860
Hey, idiots!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:44.520
Stop it! Just because I...

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:46.580
He lost! He lost! Take him down!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.120
Take him down!

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.670
Hey, referee!

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:59.020
Declare Aoyama as the winner!

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:01.410
All right.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.030
The winner is Aoyama!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.030
Way to go, Aoyama!

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.520
Rikiishi-kun...

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:44.550
Joe... You did well.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.570
I lost.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:56.650
Do your best, Kawamoto!

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:57.870
Hey, don't lose now!

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.250
You... You bastard!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.380
Hey! Where are you aiming!?

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.420
My, my, my. No matter what's said or done, this is really bad.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:10.000
My thoughts exactly. It's a combination of freestyle fighting and sloppy boxing.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:10.890
I can't bear to watch it.

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.170
But...

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:14.390
But I think it's a splendid match.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:20.130
Before we knew it, everyone decided on proper rules amongst themselves.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:25.400
The inmates, who were sent here because they couldn't abide by the rules of society,

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:29.910
are now creating and abiding by their own rules, of their own volition.

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:31.860
You're right that they're fighting with intense anger,

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:35.910
but they're learning how to fight to the end according to the rules, just like those two...

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:38.890
Just like Yabuki-kun and Rikiishi-kun!

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:42.880
That's right! It's just as you said, Miss. Just as you said!

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.380
They were moved by the blood and the countless knockdowns in Joe and Rikiishi's match.

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:54.930
They were moved so deeply that the rules were embedded in their hearts without their knowledge.

00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.050
1!

00:22:59.050 --> 00:23:00.080
2!

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:01.440
3!

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.240
Hey, Kawamoto, what's wrong?

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:04.750
Kawamoto! Stand up!

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:05.940
Stand up!

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:07.760
Fight!

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:14.690
Hey, you two! Hold your gloves tightly!

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:17.790
That way, the gloves will weigh half as much,

00:23:17.790 --> 00:23:20.520
and the power of your punches will increase!

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:41.710
I've given Joe a test,

00:24:41.710 --> 00:24:44.930
and he might feel betrayed.

00:24:44.930 --> 00:24:48.210
Now, for Joe, whose boxing soul has just awakened,

00:24:48.210 --> 00:24:49.920
which way is tomorrow!?
